1
00:00:05,705 --> 00:00:09,775
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:14,745
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:22,015
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:34,895 --> 00:00:38,905
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,135 --> 00:00:40,135
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,135 --> 00:00:41,135
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,135 --> 00:00:42,135
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:42,435 --> 00:00:46,045
(Director Woo Su Bin, Director Joo Yi Jae)

9
00:00:46,075 --> 00:00:47,245
Everyone...

10
00:00:48,245 --> 00:00:49,815
will be waiting for your cue.

11
00:00:54,685 --> 00:00:55,685
Go ahead.

12
00:01:06,625 --> 00:01:07,635
Ready.

13
00:01:11,805 --> 00:01:12,805
Action.

14
00:01:15,605 --> 00:01:16,704
Newspaper.

15
00:01:16,705 --> 00:01:17,705
(Episode 8)

16
00:01:17,706 --> 00:01:18,775
Get your newspaper.

17
00:01:19,105 --> 00:01:21,314
Hello. Please take a look.

18
00:01:21,315 --> 00:01:22,475
What do you think?

19
00:01:23,175 --> 00:01:24,884
Not beneath the lanterns of Wolhwajeong,

20
00:01:24,885 --> 00:01:26,545
but I'm here, illuminated by this moonlight.

21
00:01:27,555 --> 00:01:28,555
Well...

22
00:01:28,885 --> 00:01:31,985
From any angle, I see not one worry on you.

23
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:35,895
Let me take a look.

24
00:01:38,465 --> 00:01:40,765
No matter how I look,

25
00:01:41,595 --> 00:01:42,695
it's so beautiful.

26
00:01:46,005 --> 00:01:49,005
The me reflected in your eyes.

27
00:01:52,375 --> 00:01:54,745
Why must you always be joking?

28
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:04,625
It suits you well.

29
00:02:11,595 --> 00:02:13,065
Your smile is truly beautiful.

30
00:02:18,465 --> 00:02:19,465
Oh Ha Na.

31
00:02:22,705 --> 00:02:24,045
Everyone, wrap it up.

32
00:02:24,675 --> 00:02:25,675
Oh my...

33
00:02:27,215 --> 00:02:28,215
What's going on?

34
00:02:29,445 --> 00:02:32,715
- You, come with me. - What are you doing? That hurts.

35
00:02:32,815 --> 00:02:33,815
Oh my.

36
00:02:34,915 --> 00:02:36,085
What do you think you're doing?

37
00:02:37,785 --> 00:02:39,384
- Cut. - The ink on the contract...

38
00:02:39,385 --> 00:02:40,824
you signed isn't even dry yet.

39
00:02:40,825 --> 00:02:41,955
How dare you!

40
00:02:42,555 --> 00:02:44,295
That's enough. A lot of people are watching.

41
00:02:46,095 --> 00:02:48,065
I doubt any rumours would do you any good.

42
00:02:49,065 --> 00:02:50,764
Whether as the mother stopping the shoot...

43
00:02:50,765 --> 00:02:53,135
or the CEO who failed to renew a contract.

44
00:03:08,385 --> 00:03:09,885
Surprise.

45
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:12,825
How was my acting?

46
00:03:15,895 --> 00:03:19,495
I didn't expect Yu Geon and Director Woo to be involved.

47
00:03:21,095 --> 00:03:22,095
Right, Ha Na?

48
00:03:22,665 --> 00:03:23,935
What are you doing? Smile.

49
00:03:25,505 --> 00:03:26,565
Everyone,

50
00:03:26,935 --> 00:03:30,275
this was a surprise event that Ha Na and I prepared.

51
00:03:30,805 --> 00:03:32,075
"Gyeongseong Love Song"...

52
00:03:32,405 --> 00:03:34,715
is Ha Na's first starring role on the big screen.

53
00:03:34,745 --> 00:03:38,644
We couldn't just let it pass. If we surprised you, I'm sorry.

54
00:03:38,645 --> 00:03:39,685
Sorry.

55
00:03:42,015 --> 00:03:46,585
This was all part of a bigger plan to gift you all padded jackets.

56
00:03:47,055 --> 00:03:51,665
The temperature is about to drop, so we wanted you to film warmly.

57
00:03:51,995 --> 00:03:54,295
Director Kang over there will hand them out.

58
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:56,835
Everyone, please look after our Ha Na.

59
00:03:57,365 --> 00:03:58,365
Here they come.

60
00:04:00,935 --> 00:04:02,175
Let's take a short break.

61
00:04:02,805 --> 00:04:05,975
Hello. The jackets are here. They're free.

62
00:04:06,605 --> 00:04:07,915
Ahn Soo Hee.

63
00:04:08,275 --> 00:04:11,145
- Oh Ha Na. Ahn Soo Hee. - Oh Ha Na. Ahn Soo Hee.

64
00:04:11,285 --> 00:04:12,884
Oh Ha Na.

65
00:04:12,885 --> 00:04:15,014
- Keep warm. - Ahn Soo Hee.

66
00:04:15,015 --> 00:04:16,954
- Oh Ha Na. - I'm so embarrassed.

67
00:04:16,955 --> 00:04:18,225
Ahn Soo Hee.

68
00:04:19,455 --> 00:04:20,795
It's goose down.

69
00:04:21,395 --> 00:04:23,095
- Here you go. - Thank you.

70
00:04:23,625 --> 00:04:24,625
You're welcome.

71
00:04:25,095 --> 00:04:27,935
- We're going to move the truck. - Let's talk for a moment.

72
00:04:27,995 --> 00:04:28,995
Just what I wanted.

73
00:04:30,765 --> 00:04:33,135
Yes. Keep warm.

74
00:04:33,235 --> 00:04:35,835
Hurry, hurry and get your jackets.

75
00:04:35,905 --> 00:04:38,645
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

76
00:04:40,545 --> 00:04:41,615
I have a warm skin tone,

77
00:04:42,315 --> 00:04:43,414
so black doesn't suit me.

78
00:04:43,415 --> 00:04:46,445
- What warm tone? You're 0.1 tons. - What?

79
00:04:46,785 --> 00:04:50,555
I really thought we were wrapping up the shoot earlier.

80
00:04:50,925 --> 00:04:53,795
Seriously, who does a surprise that's so terrifying?

81
00:04:53,995 --> 00:04:56,925
- We might have to shut it down. - What?

82
00:04:57,895 --> 00:05:00,835
She pretended it was just acting, but it wasn't.

83
00:05:02,565 --> 00:05:04,405
Apparently, Seok Gi heard everything.

84
00:05:05,705 --> 00:05:07,535
That's enough. A lot of people are watching.

85
00:05:08,405 --> 00:05:10,035
I doubt any rumours would do you any good.

86
00:05:10,405 --> 00:05:12,175
Whether as the mother stopping the shoot...

87
00:05:12,605 --> 00:05:14,574
or the CEO who failed to renew a contract.

88
00:05:14,575 --> 00:05:16,115
Surprise.

89
00:05:16,475 --> 00:05:17,785
How was my acting?

90
00:05:18,215 --> 00:05:21,084
- Amazing. - Something felt off.

91
00:05:21,085 --> 00:05:23,185
After casting a top actress like Oh Ha Na,

92
00:05:23,415 --> 00:05:25,185
does it make sense that not a single article was published?

93
00:05:25,255 --> 00:05:26,725
It wasn't long ago that the article about her hiatus was released.

94
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:27,995
What? "Burnout?"

95
00:05:28,425 --> 00:05:30,155
That's ridiculous.

96
00:05:30,595 --> 00:05:34,395
Wait. So that whole event the two of them cooked up...

97
00:05:34,565 --> 00:05:35,565
was a lie?

98
00:05:36,565 --> 00:05:38,065
And without even knowing,

99
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:40,105
I was praising them for it.

100
00:05:40,235 --> 00:05:41,905
What if we get caught in the crossfire...

101
00:05:41,975 --> 00:05:43,505
of that huge mother-daughter fight?

102
00:05:43,975 --> 00:05:46,104
The production gets shut down, or our paychecks are late...

103
00:05:46,105 --> 00:05:47,745
There you are, talking nonsense again.

104
00:05:48,175 --> 00:05:50,115
The problem on our set is always you, the lighting director.

105
00:05:50,715 --> 00:05:53,815
Stop gossiping about things that haven't even happened.

106
00:05:54,055 --> 00:05:56,915
- Make sure your team keeps shut. - Yes.

107
00:05:58,355 --> 00:06:00,455
And if you go around bad-mouthing the production,

108
00:06:00,555 --> 00:06:01,725
it only reflects poorly on you, you know that?

109
00:06:01,795 --> 00:06:03,925
- Yes, I know. - We should focus on our own work.

110
00:06:04,195 --> 00:06:05,264
- Come on, let's get this set up. - Yes.

111
00:06:05,265 --> 00:06:06,925
- Let's go. - Wait up, Director.

112
00:06:08,795 --> 00:06:11,365
You all are so very clever.

113
00:06:12,005 --> 00:06:13,975
You were trying to tough it out,

114
00:06:14,035 --> 00:06:15,705
thinking I couldn't do anything once filming began.

115
00:06:16,305 --> 00:06:17,475
I am Ahn Soo Hee.

116
00:06:18,245 --> 00:06:19,674
Shut down the shoot immediately.

117
00:06:19,675 --> 00:06:21,815
Everything is on hold until I say so.

118
00:06:21,915 --> 00:06:23,144
Mom.

119
00:06:23,145 --> 00:06:26,545
You have no authority to stop the production.

120
00:06:27,815 --> 00:06:29,555
You're right. I don't.

121
00:06:29,985 --> 00:06:32,425
But while I may not have the authority, I have the power.

122
00:06:34,195 --> 00:06:35,555
I won't approve Oh Ha Na.

123
00:06:36,725 --> 00:06:38,895
I'll boycott until Oh Ha Na is dropped.

124
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,065
Sim Yu Geon, get in.

125
00:06:42,595 --> 00:06:43,595
I said, get in.

126
00:06:44,265 --> 00:06:45,365
You're not filming.

127
00:06:46,905 --> 00:06:47,905
Fine.

128
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:49,475
Then I'll...

129
00:06:51,045 --> 00:06:52,475
I'll drop out, CEO Ahn.

130
00:06:54,045 --> 00:06:55,444
- Sim Yu Geon. - Yu Geon.

131
00:06:55,445 --> 00:06:57,515
What? What you just said...

132
00:06:57,915 --> 00:07:00,545
means you'll never work in this industry again.

133
00:07:00,855 --> 00:07:01,885
Do you understand?

134
00:07:02,355 --> 00:07:03,485
I don't mind.

135
00:07:04,225 --> 00:07:05,255
After all, from the start,

136
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:07,725
this wasn't my place to begin with.

137
00:07:12,625 --> 00:07:13,625
I'm sorry, Yi Jae.

138
00:07:15,195 --> 00:07:16,195
I'm sorry to you too, Su Bin.

139
00:07:25,575 --> 00:07:26,575
Fine, then. Let's do that.

140
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:29,745
Directors, go find another male lead.

141
00:07:30,545 --> 00:07:33,385
Though it won't be easy, since our Ha Na is so notorious.

142
00:07:34,115 --> 00:07:35,085
Ma'am.

143
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:39,955
The jackets have all been handed out. And...

144
00:07:40,325 --> 00:07:42,325
the directors' jackets are with the Assistant Director...

145
00:07:44,225 --> 00:07:46,025
- Let's go. - Yes, ma'am.

146
00:07:46,365 --> 00:07:47,365
Let's go.

147
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:49,835
What are you doing?

148
00:08:04,745 --> 00:08:05,745
Ha Na.

149
00:08:06,785 --> 00:08:10,925
I told you I think ahead to what I can do in the future.

150
00:08:11,485 --> 00:08:13,055
Take this opportunity to watch and learn.

151
00:08:13,425 --> 00:08:17,255
This all happened because of your pathetic act of defiance.

152
00:08:33,475 --> 00:08:35,875
Let's just wrap for today.

153
00:08:38,715 --> 00:08:42,285
(Gyeongseong Love Song - Filming)

154
00:08:44,525 --> 00:08:46,455
I'm sorry. It's because of me.

155
00:08:50,395 --> 00:08:51,865
It's not your fault, Ha Na.

156
00:08:52,765 --> 00:08:53,765
It's okay.

157
00:09:11,085 --> 00:09:12,085
Hello.

158
00:09:12,415 --> 00:09:14,055
I'm joining the team today as a production producer.

159
00:09:14,385 --> 00:09:15,455
My name is Nam Ye Seo.

160
00:09:16,685 --> 00:09:18,725
Hello. I'm Seo In Wook, the CEO.

161
00:09:19,085 --> 00:09:20,525
(Park Jeong Hoon)

162
00:09:21,825 --> 00:09:24,225
Here are the three finalists for the role of Mu Gyeom.

163
00:09:26,095 --> 00:09:27,295
We have to choose one of them.

164
00:09:30,065 --> 00:09:31,065
You found these actors...

165
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:32,265
as if you were just waiting for this.

166
00:09:32,335 --> 00:09:34,035
Hey, it is not that I found them.

167
00:09:34,335 --> 00:09:36,235
They are the actors who expressed interest...

168
00:09:36,305 --> 00:09:37,305
before Sim Yu Geon.

169
00:09:37,445 --> 00:09:40,075
But is replacing the actor really the best option?

170
00:09:40,105 --> 00:09:41,275
It is more than the best option.

171
00:09:41,415 --> 00:09:42,875
It could actually improve the situation.

172
00:09:43,975 --> 00:09:47,915
That's right. He is the hottest guy in South Korea right now.

173
00:09:48,585 --> 00:09:49,585
Geum Seong Moo.

174
00:09:50,055 --> 00:09:51,055
Geum Seong Moo?

175
00:09:52,525 --> 00:09:54,355
- Why? - Well...

176
00:09:54,855 --> 00:09:57,155
Since he is the hottest celebrity, would he not be extremely busy?

177
00:09:57,225 --> 00:09:58,965
I am sure he has many other projects lined up.

178
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:03,495
If the script is good, actors will line up for the part.

179
00:10:03,595 --> 00:10:05,105
You are too kind.

180
00:10:05,435 --> 00:10:06,435
All right, everyone.

181
00:10:06,835 --> 00:10:09,235
We have to decide right now. Every moment we wait,

182
00:10:09,305 --> 00:10:10,475
our production budget...

183
00:10:11,245 --> 00:10:12,545
is disappearing into thin air.

184
00:10:12,775 --> 00:10:15,145
I heard Jennie and CEO Ahn secured additional funding in LA...

185
00:10:15,215 --> 00:10:17,115
while on their business trip,

186
00:10:17,175 --> 00:10:19,085
and finished pre-sales in North America and Europe, right?

187
00:10:19,945 --> 00:10:21,814
Then that means this project's significance...

188
00:10:21,815 --> 00:10:24,085
- has also changed for CEO Ahn. - That's right.

189
00:10:24,185 --> 00:10:25,354
So?

190
00:10:25,355 --> 00:10:27,385
CEO Ahn isn't dropping Sim Yu Geon.

191
00:10:29,255 --> 00:10:31,495
She was just bluffing using Sim Yu Geon.

192
00:10:31,665 --> 00:10:33,565
For what?

193
00:10:47,475 --> 00:10:50,415
(Exclusive Contract, Oh Ha Na)

194
00:10:55,385 --> 00:10:57,755
Did you not call me here to terminate my contract?

195
00:10:58,185 --> 00:10:59,185
You...

196
00:10:59,685 --> 00:11:01,895
really underestimated me.

197
00:11:02,355 --> 00:11:04,795
Did you really think you could break this contract?

198
00:11:05,995 --> 00:11:07,735
Did you forget what I said when we signed it?

199
00:11:07,935 --> 00:11:10,905
That your body and mind are all tied to this mere piece of paper.

200
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:31,685
I will renew my contract.

201
00:11:32,655 --> 00:11:33,655
Just leave Sim Yu Geon alone.

202
00:11:33,985 --> 00:11:34,995
Fine.

203
00:11:36,095 --> 00:11:37,825
The contract in his hand is yours.

204
00:11:39,025 --> 00:11:41,735
- Sign it. - You do not have to do that, Ha Na.

205
00:11:41,795 --> 00:11:43,835
I will put everything back the way it was.

206
00:11:46,405 --> 00:11:47,405
How?

207
00:11:48,035 --> 00:11:50,235
Are you being naive? Or are you just clueless?

208
00:11:50,635 --> 00:11:52,975
It was me Mom wanted from the very beginning.

209
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:56,115
And, Mom.

210
00:11:56,515 --> 00:11:58,715
I was not going to do this project because of Sim Yu Geon.

211
00:11:58,985 --> 00:12:01,615
I found the script myself and even auditioned for it.

212
00:12:02,085 --> 00:12:03,855
Sim Yu Geon just happened to be in it after I joined.

213
00:12:04,785 --> 00:12:05,785
Annoyingly enough.

214
00:12:06,085 --> 00:12:08,225
Then I guess I had good foresight.

215
00:12:08,625 --> 00:12:11,525
Taking one hostage was a good move to get you back.

216
00:12:12,525 --> 00:12:14,265
Now, give Ha Na the contract.

217
00:12:14,535 --> 00:12:15,535
Give it to me.

218
00:12:20,935 --> 00:12:23,135
(Name: Oh Ha Na)

219
00:12:30,915 --> 00:12:32,585
More than your feelings,

220
00:12:33,685 --> 00:12:35,215
I believe in the power of this paper.

221
00:12:36,585 --> 00:12:38,884
What can the two of you do together?

222
00:12:38,885 --> 00:12:40,325
You are both in the palm of my hand anyway.

223
00:12:48,565 --> 00:12:50,835
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

224
00:12:50,935 --> 00:12:52,235
Why did Nan Yeong...

225
00:12:52,565 --> 00:12:55,175
risk her own life to save Mu Gyeom?

226
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:58,605
She ran away saying she would live for herself,

227
00:12:58,675 --> 00:12:59,675
but she was so foolish.

228
00:13:01,515 --> 00:13:03,515
Maybe that was her way of saving herself.

229
00:13:04,745 --> 00:13:05,745
You know,

230
00:13:06,385 --> 00:13:07,684
they say that when you are in love,

231
00:13:07,685 --> 00:13:10,815
your eyes, nose, and lips are all turned towards that person.

232
00:13:11,555 --> 00:13:12,885
What do you think that means?

233
00:13:13,555 --> 00:13:16,795
That you look at his face more than your own,

234
00:13:17,225 --> 00:13:21,235
and eventually, when he smiles, you smile too.

235
00:13:21,995 --> 00:13:22,995
And when he cries,

236
00:13:23,765 --> 00:13:25,735
you find yourself crying too.

237
00:13:28,935 --> 00:13:30,605
Is that why this hurts so much?

238
00:13:32,345 --> 00:13:33,475
Ha Na.

239
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:36,315
I'm sorry, but can you please stop talking?

240
00:13:36,915 --> 00:13:38,385
I've already circled the Olympic Expressway three times...

241
00:13:38,445 --> 00:13:39,715
while we've been talking.

242
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:43,085
- What? - Come on...

243
00:13:43,255 --> 00:13:45,555
Sorry. Should we pull over somewhere?

244
00:13:45,725 --> 00:13:48,725
No, I can't. There's too much traffic.

245
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:51,265
Plus, Ha Na, I'm actually scared of driving.

246
00:13:53,065 --> 00:13:54,165
Where's the exit?

247
00:13:55,095 --> 00:13:56,835
Ha Na, can you press this on the GPS for me?

248
00:13:59,335 --> 00:14:00,335
I think...

249
00:14:00,805 --> 00:14:03,335
the role of Crow should be played by a well-known actor.

250
00:14:03,405 --> 00:14:05,475
- I agree. - As the independence army's leader,

251
00:14:06,005 --> 00:14:07,645
he should make an impact the moment he appears.

252
00:14:08,075 --> 00:14:09,745
Exactly. The kind of actor who makes the audience gasp...

253
00:14:09,815 --> 00:14:11,285
the moment they see him.

254
00:14:11,945 --> 00:14:14,045
But the part is so small. Won't it be hard to find someone?

255
00:14:14,285 --> 00:14:16,615
What if we offer it as a cameo?

256
00:14:17,755 --> 00:14:19,254
You're discussing the role of the independence army leader...

257
00:14:19,255 --> 00:14:20,325
who's barely in the movie?

258
00:14:20,655 --> 00:14:22,025
When we don't even have a lead actor?

259
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:23,894
We have to start with what we can.

260
00:14:23,895 --> 00:14:25,495
Aren't you just burning through the production budget?

261
00:14:25,565 --> 00:14:27,025
- Come on. - An article is out.

262
00:14:30,795 --> 00:14:31,905
Oh no...

263
00:14:34,135 --> 00:14:36,005
(Oh Ha Na And Sim Yu Geon Cast. Ian Woo's Romance Puzzle Complete?)

264
00:14:36,075 --> 00:14:39,745
Top Line must have put this out. Sim Yu Geon is in this too.

265
00:14:40,445 --> 00:14:42,545
This won't do. Let's prepare our own official press release.

266
00:14:42,615 --> 00:14:44,245
- Come here. - Yes.

267
00:14:47,785 --> 00:14:49,314
Please help me.

268
00:14:49,315 --> 00:14:50,685
Help me live as Oh Ha Na,

269
00:14:50,755 --> 00:14:51,955
and no longer as Ahn Soo Hee's daughter.

270
00:14:52,025 --> 00:14:55,025
If the first step of my independence is to become Nan Yeong,

271
00:14:55,625 --> 00:14:57,325
I think it will give me great strength.

272
00:14:59,625 --> 00:15:01,965
So much for her first step toward independence.

273
00:15:02,365 --> 00:15:04,335
Will Ha Na be okay?

274
00:15:05,035 --> 00:15:06,105
She'll be okay.

275
00:15:07,005 --> 00:15:09,035
She made the choice herself, after all.

276
00:15:09,735 --> 00:15:11,405
To protect someone precious to her.

277
00:15:15,615 --> 00:15:16,745
(Oh Ha Na And Sim Yu Geon Cast. Ian Woo's Romance Puzzle Complete?)

278
00:15:16,815 --> 00:15:17,915
(Oh Ha Na And Sim Yu Geon)

279
00:15:17,985 --> 00:15:19,085
(Who is Sim Yu Geon, Ha Na's Man?)

280
00:15:19,145 --> 00:15:20,645
(Oh Ha Na's Big Screen Debut in Ian Woo's Next Film)

281
00:15:28,555 --> 00:15:30,795
(Expiration Date: 10,000 Years)

282
00:15:36,865 --> 00:15:39,505
You were so desperate that you signed that ridiculous contract,

283
00:15:39,565 --> 00:15:41,705
so why are you trying to give it all up now?

284
00:15:45,305 --> 00:15:49,045
You need to stick right by my side and show my mom.

285
00:15:50,275 --> 00:15:52,145
Show her that there's absolutely no love between us.

286
00:17:02,785 --> 00:17:05,185
Hwa Yeon.

287
00:17:11,825 --> 00:17:13,925
Hwa Yeon.

288
00:17:15,835 --> 00:17:18,905
If she's not here, then where is she?

289
00:17:24,645 --> 00:17:28,075
When I get my hands on them, they're dead.

290
00:17:32,285 --> 00:17:33,485
Woo Su Bin.

291
00:17:34,185 --> 00:17:35,655
Woo Su Bin.

292
00:17:38,455 --> 00:17:40,085
Woo Su Bin.

293
00:17:57,505 --> 00:17:59,074
It's video evidence.

294
00:17:59,075 --> 00:18:01,005
Just in case he thought it was me.

295
00:18:05,885 --> 00:18:08,715
- It's been a while. - It's been 20 years.

296
00:18:09,485 --> 00:18:11,785
Get out in the next 20 seconds before I call the police.

297
00:18:12,725 --> 00:18:16,555
An invited guest wouldn't break down the door.

298
00:18:16,755 --> 00:18:18,095
(Emergency SOS 911)

299
00:18:20,365 --> 00:18:22,095
The same goes for you, doesn't it?

300
00:18:24,765 --> 00:18:26,765
Coming into a house when no one's home.

301
00:18:27,405 --> 00:18:28,635
But...

302
00:18:28,935 --> 00:18:30,205
why are you here?

303
00:18:31,035 --> 00:18:32,245
I...

304
00:18:32,775 --> 00:18:34,615
am funding Su Bin's movie,

305
00:18:35,245 --> 00:18:36,775
and I have urgent business to discuss with him.

306
00:18:38,245 --> 00:18:39,245
What?

307
00:18:40,045 --> 00:18:44,015
You're one crazy witch, aren't you?

308
00:18:44,085 --> 00:18:46,485
I must be a crazy witch to have dated a bastard like you...

309
00:18:46,555 --> 00:18:49,355
- without knowing you were married. - Are you still sore about that?

310
00:18:49,695 --> 00:18:51,155
You were the one who told me to get a divorce...

311
00:18:51,225 --> 00:18:52,225
because you were pregnant.

312
00:18:52,295 --> 00:18:53,365
And you stuck me in a rural one...

313
00:18:53,425 --> 00:18:54,425
so I couldn't get an abortion...

314
00:18:54,495 --> 00:18:55,835
Alright.

315
00:18:57,065 --> 00:19:00,235
I admit I made a huge mistake back then.

316
00:19:01,405 --> 00:19:02,735
You...

317
00:19:03,675 --> 00:19:05,505
could have had the baby in secret...

318
00:19:06,305 --> 00:19:08,075
and disappeared without a trace.

319
00:19:08,615 --> 00:19:10,345
No one would've thought twice about it.

320
00:19:11,815 --> 00:19:14,715
I was foolishly merciful to you.

321
00:19:20,255 --> 00:19:23,155
That's how much I liked you.

322
00:19:25,495 --> 00:19:26,895
Soo Hee.

323
00:19:27,525 --> 00:19:29,395
I'm here to repay that favour, you son of a witch.

324
00:19:43,715 --> 00:19:44,915
Good.

325
00:19:45,415 --> 00:19:46,945
It brings back old memories.

326
00:19:59,595 --> 00:20:02,065
- Then we should get going. - We should.

327
00:20:02,095 --> 00:20:03,095
Should we head to the set?

328
00:20:03,435 --> 00:20:04,435
Are you that excited?

329
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:07,105
Of course. I'm going back to the set.

330
00:20:07,765 --> 00:20:08,775
Really?

331
00:20:12,305 --> 00:20:13,305
What's going on?

332
00:20:15,745 --> 00:20:16,775
Wait here.

333
00:20:19,715 --> 00:20:20,715
Darn...

334
00:20:21,755 --> 00:20:24,385
I should've thrown you in jail back then.

335
00:20:26,525 --> 00:20:28,595
What are you two doing here?

336
00:20:31,025 --> 00:20:33,665
- Yi Jae, you should go home. - Okay.

337
00:20:35,695 --> 00:20:36,795
Woo Cheol Gyu.

338
00:20:40,305 --> 00:20:41,605
Where's your mother?

339
00:20:42,475 --> 00:20:44,505
I believe I made myself clear.

340
00:20:45,275 --> 00:20:49,115
- Never look for her again. - This time, you'd better answer me.

341
00:20:49,875 --> 00:20:51,545
Where is your mother?

342
00:20:55,285 --> 00:20:56,285
Hey.

343
00:21:02,325 --> 00:21:05,525
Are you crazy? Hitting him with this is attempted murder.

344
00:21:08,095 --> 00:21:09,995
Please leave. Both of you.

345
00:21:12,235 --> 00:21:14,435
You said you'd be a permanent stain on my name,

346
00:21:14,505 --> 00:21:16,375
and this is all you could come up with?

347
00:21:16,435 --> 00:21:18,705
Teaming up with the mother who abandoned you?

348
00:21:19,245 --> 00:21:21,775
You've really got a strong stomach.

349
00:21:22,545 --> 00:21:24,244
What? How dare an inhuman bastard like you...

350
00:21:24,245 --> 00:21:25,845
spout such nonsense?

351
00:21:26,115 --> 00:21:28,555
I haven't lived a single day as Woo Su Bin's mother,

352
00:21:28,615 --> 00:21:30,415
so why do you keep calling me that?

353
00:21:31,015 --> 00:21:34,285
- I came here as Oh Ha Na's mother. - Exactly.

354
00:21:35,495 --> 00:21:36,925
So please leave.

355
00:21:37,955 --> 00:21:40,195
You both have nothing to do with me.

356
00:21:41,835 --> 00:21:42,965
Then,

357
00:21:44,535 --> 00:21:46,305
what about the woman you call Mother?

358
00:21:46,535 --> 00:21:49,174
Are you going to make her live her whole life...

359
00:21:49,175 --> 00:21:50,275
always on the run like you?

360
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:54,075
My mother isn't on the run. I'm protecting her.

361
00:22:11,665 --> 00:22:13,925
If you want to see your mother's face in one piece,

362
00:22:14,225 --> 00:22:15,895
send her back before it's too late.

363
00:22:24,845 --> 00:22:27,045
I regret ever fixing you.

364
00:22:28,675 --> 00:22:31,945
I guess once something is broken,

365
00:22:32,315 --> 00:22:35,515
- it's hard to be whole again. - Father.

366
00:22:37,515 --> 00:22:41,355
That's right. Just because you fixed my leg,

367
00:22:41,425 --> 00:22:43,255
it didn't make my life whole again.

368
00:22:43,925 --> 00:22:46,195
The one who made my life whole again...

369
00:22:47,195 --> 00:22:48,465
was Su Bin.

370
00:23:06,445 --> 00:23:08,385
Is that man still living like that?

371
00:23:09,015 --> 00:23:11,625
And you... Are you still living like this?

372
00:23:12,755 --> 00:23:15,295
I didn't come here to see such a pathetic sight.

373
00:23:15,825 --> 00:23:16,825
You.

374
00:23:17,925 --> 00:23:20,065
What was your ulterior motive for casting my Ha Na?

375
00:23:21,065 --> 00:23:23,265
Did you come all this way just to ask me that?

376
00:23:24,435 --> 00:23:26,635
What kind of ulterior motive do you think I have?

377
00:23:27,735 --> 00:23:28,974
You wouldn't budge back then...

378
00:23:28,975 --> 00:23:30,605
no matter how much I pushed her on you.

379
00:23:31,105 --> 00:23:33,004
So why did you cast her the moment she left my side...

380
00:23:33,005 --> 00:23:34,305
as if to show me up?

381
00:23:36,375 --> 00:23:37,945
My father and you...

382
00:23:39,145 --> 00:23:40,645
You two are quite alike.

383
00:23:40,915 --> 00:23:42,715
- What? - That's probably why...

384
00:23:43,355 --> 00:23:45,085
Oh Ha Na and I have something in common.

385
00:23:45,485 --> 00:23:46,955
Even though we never lived together.

386
00:23:47,185 --> 00:23:48,254
Hey.

387
00:23:48,255 --> 00:23:50,555
This is exactly why I came.

388
00:23:50,795 --> 00:23:52,024
Just because you have a little of my blood,

389
00:23:52,025 --> 00:23:53,064
don't you dare go to my Ha Na...

390
00:23:53,065 --> 00:23:55,635
and start spouting that nonsense about being siblings or family.

391
00:23:56,635 --> 00:23:58,465
If you do, even I don't know what I'll be capable of.

392
00:23:58,605 --> 00:24:02,175
It's just a director casting an actor for a movie,

393
00:24:03,335 --> 00:24:04,905
but you're really reading a lot into it.

394
00:24:06,575 --> 00:24:08,345
This is a critical time for my Ha Na.

395
00:24:09,545 --> 00:24:12,445
So don't get caught up in any unnecessary drama,

396
00:24:12,515 --> 00:24:13,615
and until the end,

397
00:24:13,685 --> 00:24:15,755
just focus on making a good movie, Director.

398
00:24:38,505 --> 00:24:41,445
Su Bin, are you okay?

399
00:24:43,275 --> 00:24:45,515
Yi Jae, I'm sorry.

400
00:24:46,885 --> 00:24:48,085
Just give me a moment.

401
00:25:27,425 --> 00:25:28,725
Woo Su Bin.

402
00:26:00,455 --> 00:26:02,995
All happy families are alike,

403
00:26:03,925 --> 00:26:05,465
but every unhappy family...

404
00:26:07,095 --> 00:26:09,035
is unhappy in its own way.

405
00:26:09,295 --> 00:26:11,905
Hello? Are you Su Bin?

406
00:26:12,335 --> 00:26:15,235
Say hello. This is your aunt.

407
00:26:15,575 --> 00:26:16,735
And your uncle.

408
00:26:17,205 --> 00:26:18,674
- Hello. - Hi.

409
00:26:18,675 --> 00:26:20,105
The source of my family's unhappiness...

410
00:26:20,645 --> 00:26:21,745
was me.

411
00:26:28,815 --> 00:26:29,855
Look.

412
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:31,255
It's Ahn Soo Hee.

413
00:26:32,085 --> 00:26:34,385
(Soo Hee's Journal)

414
00:26:35,525 --> 00:26:36,525
Look.

415
00:26:37,325 --> 00:26:39,225
The older he gets, the more he looks like Ahn Soo Hee.

416
00:26:40,595 --> 00:26:42,535
Is he really Ahn Soo Hee's child?

417
00:26:43,395 --> 00:26:45,835
Then that means Cheol Gyu and Ahn Soo Hee...

418
00:26:47,335 --> 00:26:48,975
Hwa Yeon is something else.

419
00:26:49,675 --> 00:26:52,675
How could she raise a child her husband had with someone else?

420
00:26:53,675 --> 00:26:55,345
What an ignorant thing to say.

421
00:26:55,415 --> 00:26:57,875
How dare they say that in front of the child?

422
00:26:58,715 --> 00:27:00,045
I'm sorry.

423
00:27:01,215 --> 00:27:02,615
I'm sorry.

424
00:27:04,215 --> 00:27:05,625
Su Bin...

425
00:27:06,155 --> 00:27:07,725
is my son.

426
00:27:12,925 --> 00:27:15,095
If you want to go see your family that badly,

427
00:27:15,695 --> 00:27:16,695
then go by yourself.

428
00:27:16,935 --> 00:27:18,805
And don't even think about coming back.

429
00:27:20,135 --> 00:27:22,305
No.

430
00:27:23,435 --> 00:27:25,505
I won't go again.

431
00:27:27,005 --> 00:27:28,205
I mean it.

432
00:27:32,185 --> 00:27:33,385
That's when I realised.

433
00:27:36,215 --> 00:27:40,055
- Some smiles... - Son, are you awake?

434
00:27:40,425 --> 00:27:42,155
look just like crying.

435
00:27:44,325 --> 00:27:46,195
Whenever Mom looked at me,

436
00:27:47,095 --> 00:27:48,295
she was crying.

437
00:28:09,015 --> 00:28:10,055
Hey, you.

438
00:28:16,425 --> 00:28:18,295
Mom, who is that?

439
00:28:21,625 --> 00:28:24,235
Ha Na, get in the car. Now.

440
00:28:33,675 --> 00:28:34,675
Who are you?

441
00:28:36,245 --> 00:28:38,545
Hello. I'm Woo Su Bin.

442
00:28:45,755 --> 00:28:48,625
What do you think you're doing here? Who sent you?

443
00:28:49,255 --> 00:28:51,825
Did Woo Cheol Gyu send you? Or was it that woman?

444
00:28:52,165 --> 00:28:54,295
Why? Are they saying they can't raise you anymore?

445
00:28:54,525 --> 00:28:55,635
I came on my own.

446
00:28:55,695 --> 00:28:58,165
My mom cries every day because of me.

447
00:28:58,705 --> 00:29:01,335
If I'm not around, my dad won't get angry,

448
00:29:01,405 --> 00:29:02,905
and I don't think my mom will cry anymore.

449
00:29:02,975 --> 00:29:05,605
- So what do you want from me? - Please take me in.

450
00:29:06,475 --> 00:29:08,815
I get good grades. And I'm a good listener.

451
00:29:08,975 --> 00:29:12,515
If you'll just take me in, I promise I'll grow up well.

452
00:29:13,445 --> 00:29:15,815
- Where's your home? Let's go there. - No. I'm not going.

453
00:29:15,885 --> 00:29:18,755
- Hey, you. - Please, take me in. Please?

454
00:29:18,825 --> 00:29:22,295
- Be quiet. - Please. Okay? Please.

455
00:29:22,555 --> 00:29:23,754
Be quiet.

456
00:29:23,755 --> 00:29:27,095
Please take me in.

457
00:29:27,625 --> 00:29:29,795
Please take me in.

458
00:29:31,035 --> 00:29:32,805
Be quiet. Quiet.

459
00:29:32,835 --> 00:29:36,475
- Please take me in. Please. - Please.

460
00:29:49,585 --> 00:29:50,585
Get out.

461
00:29:56,355 --> 00:29:58,665
Are you crazy? This is why he came to me.

462
00:29:59,265 --> 00:30:01,665
He's asking me to raise him. Does that make any sense?

463
00:30:01,925 --> 00:30:04,565
Perfect. Then you can raise him.

464
00:30:04,935 --> 00:30:07,335
I don't want that unruly kid either.

465
00:30:08,065 --> 00:30:10,435
Honey, I have a family of my own now.

466
00:30:10,675 --> 00:30:12,675
How can I just suddenly raise him?

467
00:30:13,375 --> 00:30:16,275
- Mom. - Hey, I told you I'm not your mom.

468
00:30:16,945 --> 00:30:18,445
Come here, Su Bin.

469
00:30:24,085 --> 00:30:26,185
Where have you been?

470
00:30:27,355 --> 00:30:30,095
Mom was so worried.

471
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:32,265
I was just...

472
00:30:32,895 --> 00:30:35,765
I felt like I was the one making you cry.

473
00:30:37,935 --> 00:30:42,005
Su Bin, you make Mom cry,

474
00:30:42,305 --> 00:30:45,235
and you also make her smile like you are now.

475
00:30:46,045 --> 00:30:47,605
Because you're my son.

476
00:30:52,485 --> 00:30:55,755
- Mom. - Don't cry.

477
00:31:14,505 --> 00:31:15,735
After that day,

478
00:31:16,905 --> 00:31:19,545
my world felt like nothing but complete darkness.

479
00:31:26,845 --> 00:31:29,385
Just when I thought I'd rather stay in the darkness,

480
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:34,685
I met you.

481
00:31:38,655 --> 00:31:40,895
Why does this story end with you?

482
00:31:42,465 --> 00:31:43,565
Maybe...

483
00:31:44,995 --> 00:31:47,065
it's because the first person who brought light into my world...

484
00:31:48,305 --> 00:31:49,675
was you.

485
00:31:52,645 --> 00:31:53,645
Woo Su Bin.

486
00:31:56,115 --> 00:31:57,615
Thanks to you,

487
00:31:58,745 --> 00:32:00,345
all my bad memories...

488
00:32:01,115 --> 00:32:02,755
have turned into love.

489
00:32:04,685 --> 00:32:09,195
My scars have now become a reminder of how much I liked you,

490
00:32:10,225 --> 00:32:11,355
and the movie...

491
00:32:12,365 --> 00:32:14,095
is no longer an unfulfilled dream,

492
00:32:15,095 --> 00:32:17,095
but a dream we're dreaming together.

493
00:32:19,735 --> 00:32:21,105
When it rains,

494
00:32:23,805 --> 00:32:25,745
I don't think of the day we broke up.

495
00:32:26,745 --> 00:32:28,775
Instead, I remember the day we kissed.

496
00:32:32,445 --> 00:32:33,585
That's what you mean to me.

497
00:32:34,485 --> 00:32:36,485
How could you not be love to me?

498
00:32:42,625 --> 00:32:46,195
You're the greatest comfort of my life.

499
00:32:47,095 --> 00:32:48,095
Really?

500
00:33:53,295 --> 00:33:54,525
Sorry.

501
00:33:55,095 --> 00:33:57,535
It's been a long time since I had someone next to me.

502
00:34:01,235 --> 00:34:02,235
What?

503
00:34:03,005 --> 00:34:05,605
What time is it? Can I sleep in a little?

504
00:34:07,645 --> 00:34:08,645
A long time?

505
00:34:12,145 --> 00:34:13,715
Just wake me up later.

506
00:34:16,885 --> 00:34:18,285
You said it's been a long time?

507
00:34:19,255 --> 00:34:20,555
I don't know.

508
00:34:24,495 --> 00:34:28,095
- How long has it been? - What's gotten into you this early?

509
00:34:29,035 --> 00:34:32,035
No, I mean, how long has it been?

510
00:34:32,605 --> 00:34:34,505
- I don't know. - Hey, Joo Yi Jae.

511
00:34:34,565 --> 00:34:36,074
- Why? - Hey.

512
00:34:36,075 --> 00:34:38,774
- What? - Joo Yi Jae. I'm asking you.

513
00:34:38,775 --> 00:34:40,175
- That tickles. - I'm asking you.

514
00:34:40,575 --> 00:34:42,915
- I'm asking. - That tickles.

515
00:34:47,245 --> 00:34:49,615
That love you said was like a war,

516
00:34:50,985 --> 00:34:52,085
was it with that guy?

517
00:34:54,685 --> 00:34:57,155
He was also really good at peeling apples.

518
00:34:57,625 --> 00:34:58,625
What?

519
00:34:59,095 --> 00:35:00,395
Open wide.

520
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:03,695
How good was he?

521
00:35:04,095 --> 00:35:05,765
Could he make a rabbit like this one?

522
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:09,275
So today's the day we film that scene, right?

523
00:35:09,305 --> 00:35:11,375
Where Nan Yeong falls for Mu Gyeom at first sight.

524
00:35:11,535 --> 00:35:13,144
I'm looking forward to it.

525
00:35:13,145 --> 00:35:15,615
Why? Did you fall in love with that guy at first sight?

526
00:35:16,275 --> 00:35:18,715
Seriously, how long are you going to keep this up?

527
00:35:18,775 --> 00:35:20,085
When are you going to tell me?

528
00:35:20,145 --> 00:35:22,245
Look, I'm telling you we only dated for a short time.

529
00:35:23,385 --> 00:35:27,085
- He was an acting student... - He must have been handsome then?

530
00:35:28,225 --> 00:35:29,355
You know I have a thing for looks.

531
00:35:31,055 --> 00:35:33,295
But he was only handsome back then. Now... not so much.

532
00:35:33,425 --> 00:35:36,535
Do you two still keep in touch?

533
00:35:36,595 --> 00:35:40,865
No, I mean, since we dated in college,

534
00:35:40,935 --> 00:35:42,105
we just run into each other,

535
00:35:42,165 --> 00:35:44,275
and we all know each other through mutual friends.

536
00:35:44,335 --> 00:35:47,544
Anyway, he helped me out whenever I was filming a club movie,

537
00:35:47,545 --> 00:35:49,814
so we just ended up running into dating. It was nothing special.

538
00:35:49,815 --> 00:35:52,614
That part is the most important. Why would you leave it out?

539
00:35:52,615 --> 00:35:54,714
Maybe it's because I can't remember that important part,

540
00:35:54,715 --> 00:35:55,914
that the romance wasn't that special.

541
00:35:55,915 --> 00:35:57,455
I heard it was a life-or-death romance.

542
00:35:57,515 --> 00:35:59,685
Did you kill him? Just answer that.

543
00:36:01,455 --> 00:36:03,894
Yes. I killed him.

544
00:36:03,895 --> 00:36:04,895
Very brutally.

545
00:36:07,725 --> 00:36:11,965
- Am I the only one with a past? - I don't have one.

546
00:36:12,505 --> 00:36:14,134
- Really? - Even if I did,

547
00:36:14,135 --> 00:36:17,105
I wouldn't tell you. I consider that being polite to you.

548
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:19,875
What? Why are you making me out to be the rude one?

549
00:36:20,205 --> 00:36:23,875
- You're the one who kept prying. - You take the bait every time.

550
00:36:27,415 --> 00:36:29,714
- You really don't? Tell me. - I don't.

551
00:36:29,715 --> 00:36:32,215
- Was she prettier than me? - It's very dangerous.

552
00:36:32,855 --> 00:36:33,885
Why you...

553
00:36:33,925 --> 00:36:36,655
- Director, hello. - Hello.

554
00:36:37,955 --> 00:36:39,994
- Hello. - Hello.

555
00:36:39,995 --> 00:36:43,095
- Good morning, Directors. - What are you doing?

556
00:36:43,195 --> 00:36:46,065
We've already caught three couples on set.

557
00:36:46,365 --> 00:36:47,964
They should be working, but instead...

558
00:36:47,965 --> 00:36:49,905
Darn it.

559
00:36:51,435 --> 00:36:52,875
Make that four couples...

560
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:56,115
But I heard that when a lot of couples form,

561
00:36:56,175 --> 00:36:57,615
it means the set has a great atmosphere.

562
00:36:58,045 --> 00:37:02,485
Who said that? Who? It's only great for them.

563
00:37:02,815 --> 00:37:05,085
Directors, If you witness...

564
00:37:05,455 --> 00:37:06,455
any romantic behaviour between the staff members,

565
00:37:06,456 --> 00:37:07,525
please report it to me immediately.

566
00:37:07,685 --> 00:37:09,825
- I'll go get things ready. - Okay.

567
00:37:18,665 --> 00:37:21,065
(No Dating On Set)

568
00:37:26,575 --> 00:37:31,045
(No Smoking On Set)

569
00:37:45,455 --> 00:37:48,225
"When you fall in love..."

570
00:38:13,755 --> 00:38:15,655
Hey, you're going to drool.

571
00:38:16,895 --> 00:38:19,595
Change how you look at Nan Yeong.

572
00:38:19,625 --> 00:38:21,795
You can't have that look of love yet.

573
00:38:21,865 --> 00:38:24,635
What? What do you mean? You're wrong.

574
00:38:24,995 --> 00:38:26,734
Director Joo.

575
00:38:26,735 --> 00:38:29,475
Erase all your worries and pain.

576
00:38:29,535 --> 00:38:31,805
Right now, you're Mu Gyeom, a carefree young master.

577
00:38:31,835 --> 00:38:33,875
Not an independence fighter. Got it?

578
00:38:35,875 --> 00:38:38,014
- Please keep doing it like that. - Yes.

579
00:38:38,015 --> 00:38:39,345
Thank you.

580
00:38:42,245 --> 00:38:44,655
Mu Gyeom, let's talk for a second.

581
00:38:46,885 --> 00:38:48,725
- Now. - Yes.

582
00:38:50,595 --> 00:38:52,565
How are you feeling? Are you okay?

583
00:38:53,095 --> 00:38:54,095
Of course.

584
00:38:55,195 --> 00:38:56,195
Director.

585
00:38:57,895 --> 00:39:01,305
No matter how much it seems like I'm back to my old self,

586
00:39:01,635 --> 00:39:03,775
I'm not the same Oh Ha Na I used to be.

587
00:39:04,305 --> 00:39:05,845
I've been reborn.

588
00:39:06,875 --> 00:39:09,475
- I'm on my second life now. - Happy birthday.

589
00:39:10,345 --> 00:39:12,715
Even if I had run away from Wolhwajeong,

590
00:39:13,345 --> 00:39:16,815
a world without Mu Gyeom would be meaningless, right?

591
00:39:18,155 --> 00:39:21,785
Is that why Nan Yeong threw herself to save him?

592
00:39:22,085 --> 00:39:23,294
Exactly.

593
00:39:23,295 --> 00:39:26,895
I signed the contract to protect myself.

594
00:39:34,635 --> 00:39:35,835
Come here.

595
00:39:36,475 --> 00:39:38,035
Who is Yi Jae's ex-boyfriend?

596
00:39:38,535 --> 00:39:40,945
- What? Her ex-boyfriend? - Shh.

597
00:39:41,875 --> 00:39:43,345
Keep your voice down.

598
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:45,815
Which ex-boyfriend are you talking about, exactly?

599
00:39:46,185 --> 00:39:48,585
- There's more than one? - You think there'd only be one?

600
00:39:49,285 --> 00:39:50,985
Just the ones I've seen...

601
00:39:59,095 --> 00:40:00,095
Never mind.

602
00:40:02,795 --> 00:40:05,735
There is a really famous actor among them, though.

603
00:40:09,635 --> 00:40:10,635
Who?

604
00:40:13,305 --> 00:40:14,305
No, forget it.

605
00:40:15,975 --> 00:40:17,375
I don't want to know.

606
00:40:18,415 --> 00:40:19,415
What's with him?

607
00:40:30,625 --> 00:40:32,155
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

608
00:40:39,935 --> 00:40:42,905
That's perfect. The look of someone in love.

609
00:40:43,375 --> 00:40:45,304
- What? - We'll start the rehearsal now.

610
00:40:45,305 --> 00:40:47,175
Let's begin the rehearsal.

611
00:40:49,945 --> 00:40:52,175
- Okay. - There's too much coming in.

612
00:40:52,445 --> 00:40:53,715
Okay, let's get ready now.

613
00:40:53,785 --> 00:40:54,785
- Okay. - Okay.

614
00:40:57,215 --> 00:40:58,355
Ready.

615
00:40:59,185 --> 00:41:00,255
Action.

616
00:41:00,755 --> 00:41:04,255
- I have never seen you before. - I am Nan Yeong.

617
00:41:09,435 --> 00:41:10,435
What are you doing?

618
00:41:11,165 --> 00:41:12,595
You're supposed to grab my wrist.

619
00:41:17,205 --> 00:41:19,275
If you grab it like that, are you a scholar or a playboy?

620
00:41:21,805 --> 00:41:23,144
Check it again.

621
00:41:23,145 --> 00:41:24,745
Memorize every single detail.

622
00:41:26,215 --> 00:41:27,385
I'm sorry.

623
00:41:28,245 --> 00:41:29,245
I'm sorry.

624
00:41:31,585 --> 00:41:33,425
- I'm sorry. - It's fine.

625
00:41:33,885 --> 00:41:35,925
- What do we do? - I'm sorry.

626
00:41:35,995 --> 00:41:37,825
It's fine. We'll see.

627
00:41:39,225 --> 00:41:41,425
Okay, let's go again.

628
00:41:41,495 --> 00:41:43,735
Let's focus a little more and try again.

629
00:41:44,065 --> 00:41:45,165
Ready.

630
00:41:45,695 --> 00:41:46,805
Action.

631
00:41:48,635 --> 00:41:50,175
I have never seen you before.

632
00:41:51,275 --> 00:41:52,945
I am Nan Yeong.

633
00:42:01,345 --> 00:42:03,285
The temper of a young master from a noble family...

634
00:42:04,255 --> 00:42:05,584
is quite short.

635
00:42:05,585 --> 00:42:07,355
Is there a reason I should not be?

636
00:42:08,855 --> 00:42:12,495
When you have a face so in love.

637
00:42:16,435 --> 00:42:17,565
Relax.

638
00:42:18,235 --> 00:42:20,965
Cut. Good. We'll go with that.

639
00:42:30,575 --> 00:42:31,575
We're like...

640
00:42:32,075 --> 00:42:33,745
connected in a way...

641
00:42:36,385 --> 00:42:37,855
Oh, you're impossible.

642
00:42:43,555 --> 00:42:45,395
The spa date has ended.

643
00:42:45,955 --> 00:42:48,725
Of the two people you went on a date with today,

644
00:42:48,795 --> 00:42:51,765
go to the room of the person you find more appealing.

645
00:42:54,565 --> 00:42:55,565
What?

646
00:43:37,145 --> 00:43:38,275
Seo In Wook.

647
00:43:41,085 --> 00:43:42,445
I don't sleep with a guy a second time...

648
00:43:42,515 --> 00:43:43,755
if we got drunk and slept together.

649
00:43:43,915 --> 00:43:46,225
It might seem like a crappy rule to some,

650
00:43:46,285 --> 00:43:49,595
but I've tried my best to live by it.

651
00:43:51,455 --> 00:43:52,965
But just now,

652
00:43:53,865 --> 00:43:55,295
between you and me, In Wook,

653
00:43:56,065 --> 00:43:57,665
a second night happened.

654
00:43:58,365 --> 00:43:59,865
What do you think that means?

655
00:44:00,605 --> 00:44:02,835
That there will be a third and a fourth night?

656
00:44:03,435 --> 00:44:04,435
And more?

657
00:44:10,345 --> 00:44:11,345
Okay.

658
00:44:11,915 --> 00:44:14,245
- I'm quitting the show. - No.

659
00:44:14,515 --> 00:44:15,515
Don't.

660
00:44:16,515 --> 00:44:18,985
- What? - Our third time...

661
00:44:19,685 --> 00:44:21,555
will be after this shoot is over.

662
00:44:22,155 --> 00:44:25,395
So stay on as the Catfish Man until the end.

663
00:44:28,065 --> 00:44:29,465
As the man everyone desires.

664
00:44:32,165 --> 00:44:35,165
- Wait, what are you talking about? - You have five minutes left.

665
00:44:36,805 --> 00:44:38,805
Have a good date.

666
00:44:47,485 --> 00:44:49,085
She's a really strange woman.

667
00:44:51,715 --> 00:44:52,715
I love her.

668
00:44:53,955 --> 00:44:57,155
- Please wrap up within 30 minutes. - Okay.

669
00:44:57,225 --> 00:45:00,825
- The team dinner is optional. - Okay.

670
00:45:00,895 --> 00:45:02,994
I've shared the location in the team chat room.

671
00:45:02,995 --> 00:45:05,335
- Please check it. - Okay.

672
00:45:08,265 --> 00:45:10,675
Directors. For the Crow cameo,

673
00:45:11,435 --> 00:45:13,375
we got actor Geum Seong Moo.

674
00:45:14,905 --> 00:45:16,075
Isn't that great?

675
00:45:19,715 --> 00:45:21,845
Wait, Geum Seong Moo?

676
00:45:22,885 --> 00:45:23,885
That's great.

677
00:45:25,015 --> 00:45:26,015
Oh, right.

678
00:45:26,285 --> 00:45:28,585
Assistant Director. Hey, about what I mentioned earlier...

679
00:45:30,925 --> 00:45:32,355
This can't be good.

680
00:45:36,465 --> 00:45:38,265
- Cheers. - Cheers.

681
00:45:43,575 --> 00:45:44,575
Cheers.

682
00:45:49,005 --> 00:45:50,375
Is the beer good?

683
00:45:50,545 --> 00:45:53,185
Come on, just have one drink. It's okay.

684
00:45:55,015 --> 00:45:56,555
I'll just stick to a soft drink.

685
00:46:08,225 --> 00:46:09,795
- Did you see that? - See what?

686
00:46:20,275 --> 00:46:22,875
But are we really going with Geum Seong Moo for the cameo?

687
00:46:23,115 --> 00:46:25,675
- Why? - I did a drama with him,

688
00:46:25,745 --> 00:46:29,145
and I'm just not sure he's a good fit for Crow.

689
00:46:29,285 --> 00:46:30,985
Looks like you didn't get along with him again.

690
00:46:31,915 --> 00:46:33,985
- "Again?" - I heard you always have trouble...

691
00:46:34,055 --> 00:46:35,055
with your male co-stars.

692
00:46:35,425 --> 00:46:37,525
Getting along with your co-stars is a skill too.

693
00:46:37,755 --> 00:46:40,195
That just gave me chills. You sound just like my mom.

694
00:46:43,165 --> 00:46:45,565
If he was worth getting along with, I would have.

695
00:46:46,405 --> 00:46:47,464
What do you think I am,

696
00:46:47,465 --> 00:46:49,205
some thug who picks fights everywhere?

697
00:46:49,705 --> 00:46:51,905
See? She gets along just fine with Mu Gyeom, right?

698
00:46:53,475 --> 00:46:55,105
Hey, that's your sixth one.

699
00:46:56,845 --> 00:46:58,345
You need to watch yourself while we're filming.

700
00:46:58,945 --> 00:47:00,545
Think those natural good looks will last forever?

701
00:47:01,545 --> 00:47:04,415
- I'm sorry, Senior. - Stop with the "Senior" already.

702
00:47:05,715 --> 00:47:06,885
You call that getting along?

703
00:47:07,355 --> 00:47:08,355
She's being nice.

704
00:47:10,155 --> 00:47:13,925
Still, I bet you're happy, Junior. You're a big fan of Geum Seong Moo.

705
00:47:19,095 --> 00:47:20,664
You mean the Hong Kong actor Takeshi Kaneshiro?

706
00:47:20,665 --> 00:47:23,575
His last name is Kaneshiro and his first name is Takeshi.

707
00:47:25,335 --> 00:47:27,705
So what? The Geum Seong Moo here has the last name Geum...

708
00:47:27,775 --> 00:47:29,005
and the first name Seong Moo.

709
00:47:29,205 --> 00:47:31,175
- Is that his real name? - Yes, it is.

710
00:47:35,015 --> 00:47:36,015
You seem to know a lot about him.

711
00:47:36,515 --> 00:47:39,415
What? Director Joo, are you a fan of Geum Seong Moo too?

712
00:47:40,085 --> 00:47:42,425
I'm so disappointed.

713
00:47:42,825 --> 00:47:44,724
My show, "Contract Marriage," was on at the same time as his,

714
00:47:44,725 --> 00:47:46,055
and he completely crushed me in the ratings.

715
00:47:46,225 --> 00:47:47,625
Is that right?

716
00:47:47,995 --> 00:47:50,865
Right. Geum Seong Moo became a star because of that drama.

717
00:47:50,995 --> 00:47:53,205
Is there anyone who isn't a fan of Geum Seong Moo these days?

718
00:47:55,005 --> 00:47:56,005
Good for you.

719
00:47:57,135 --> 00:47:58,505
Let's keep business and pleasure separate.

720
00:47:59,035 --> 00:48:00,675
You seem to be the one having the most trouble with that.

721
00:48:00,745 --> 00:48:02,745
I suppose you're good at separating them, Junior.

722
00:48:06,145 --> 00:48:08,445
I'm trying, Senior.

723
00:48:10,985 --> 00:48:12,555
Well, I should be going.

724
00:48:15,425 --> 00:48:16,525
Chae Yeon, let's go.

725
00:48:19,725 --> 00:48:21,464
- Okay, see you. - Take care.

726
00:48:21,465 --> 00:48:22,495
Goodbye, everyone.

727
00:48:22,795 --> 00:48:24,165
Why did she even come to the team dinner?

728
00:48:25,095 --> 00:48:26,295
To pick a fight, I guess.

729
00:48:26,805 --> 00:48:29,704
- Mu Gyeom, have a drink with me. - Good.

730
00:48:29,705 --> 00:48:31,075
It's fine, right, Directors?

731
00:48:31,935 --> 00:48:34,005
- Just a little for Mu Gyeom. - Just a little.

732
00:48:34,075 --> 00:48:35,075
Just a little.

733
00:48:35,775 --> 00:48:37,645
And a lot for me.

734
00:48:38,575 --> 00:48:39,575
Cheers.

735
00:48:49,325 --> 00:48:51,095
I told you to only have a little.

736
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:53,265
Another bottle of soju over here.

737
00:49:00,365 --> 00:49:02,505
That Sim Yu Geon...

738
00:49:03,235 --> 00:49:05,335
Even I have to work this hard to maintain my natural gifts.

739
00:49:07,145 --> 00:49:10,145
Does he think it's easy to maintain this dewy glow?

740
00:49:11,575 --> 00:49:13,715
- Assistant Director. - What?

741
00:49:13,785 --> 00:49:15,085
Seriously.

742
00:49:15,645 --> 00:49:17,615
- What's going on? - This is great.

743
00:49:17,685 --> 00:49:20,325
- Assistant Director, come on in. - This is great.

744
00:49:20,385 --> 00:49:23,395
- I can't go. - Come on, Assistant Director.

745
00:49:24,095 --> 00:49:25,255
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

746
00:49:25,825 --> 00:49:29,295
Look, I already told you, Jennie.

747
00:49:32,995 --> 00:49:34,405
And he's been drinking too?

748
00:49:35,435 --> 00:49:37,805
- Listen to me... - So you're hungry again?

749
00:49:37,875 --> 00:49:39,875
- Feeling so good. - Should we have another round?

750
00:49:39,945 --> 00:49:41,874
Hey, let's go this way.

751
00:49:41,875 --> 00:49:42,905
Good night!

752
00:49:42,975 --> 00:49:44,545
- Bye. - Bye.

753
00:49:44,615 --> 00:49:45,615
Good night!

754
00:49:47,515 --> 00:49:48,515
Want to go for a walk?

755
00:49:48,585 --> 00:49:51,855
Anyone I catch going for a walk tonight is dead meat.

756
00:49:55,355 --> 00:49:57,055
I'll just come to your room later.

757
00:49:57,355 --> 00:49:59,095
A nighttime walk is innocent enough.

758
00:49:59,725 --> 00:50:01,965
We need to patrol these hallways.

759
00:50:02,825 --> 00:50:03,835
That's right.

760
00:50:04,365 --> 00:50:07,505
I'm sure there's at least one couple on our floor.

761
00:50:08,405 --> 00:50:09,405
Really?

762
00:50:11,005 --> 00:50:12,005
You're sharp.

763
00:50:12,905 --> 00:50:15,105
Ye Seo, do you want to take the lower floors?

764
00:50:15,445 --> 00:50:16,775
I'll take the upper floors.

765
00:50:17,175 --> 00:50:18,175
Me?

766
00:50:19,015 --> 00:50:20,245
I'd rather not.

767
00:50:21,045 --> 00:50:22,545
Weren't you against on-set romances?

768
00:50:23,755 --> 00:50:25,585
I tend to discourage it,

769
00:50:26,055 --> 00:50:29,255
but can you really stop people from falling in love?

770
00:50:29,825 --> 00:50:31,994
Right, just leave them alone.

771
00:50:31,995 --> 00:50:33,995
They'll all break up once filming is over anyway.

772
00:50:34,495 --> 00:50:36,795
Exactly. They're just going to break up anyway,

773
00:50:37,095 --> 00:50:38,935
so why do they have to do it at work?

774
00:50:39,905 --> 00:50:41,065
They're so dead.

775
00:50:42,905 --> 00:50:44,405
- Good night. - Good night.

776
00:50:44,475 --> 00:50:45,875
- Get home safe. - Good work.

777
00:50:45,935 --> 00:50:47,444
Good night.

778
00:50:47,445 --> 00:50:49,405
- I'll to take a shower. - Okay.

779
00:50:49,575 --> 00:50:50,975
The doors are closing.

780
00:50:52,375 --> 00:50:53,385
Hey.

781
00:50:54,985 --> 00:50:56,714
Isn't he way too drunk?

782
00:50:56,715 --> 00:50:58,215
I think we should take him to his room.

783
00:50:58,615 --> 00:50:59,925
What, is he a baby?

784
00:51:00,485 --> 00:51:02,355
Sim Yu Geon, what's your floor?

785
00:51:02,725 --> 00:51:04,695
- Sixth floor. - Oh my goodness.

786
00:51:04,755 --> 00:51:06,225
- The doors are opening. - Let's go.

787
00:51:06,295 --> 00:51:07,295
No, hey.

788
00:51:08,025 --> 00:51:09,395
Hey.

789
00:51:11,995 --> 00:51:13,235
Woo Su Bin.

790
00:51:13,905 --> 00:51:16,065
You're so dead when Seong Moo gets here.

791
00:51:26,845 --> 00:51:28,385
Wait. Where's your key card?

792
00:51:29,545 --> 00:51:30,555
It's right here.

793
00:53:01,475 --> 00:53:04,075
Seriously, why won't it open?

794
00:53:05,275 --> 00:53:07,245
Come on.

795
00:53:16,255 --> 00:53:17,395
Is it a ghost?

796
00:53:30,905 --> 00:53:33,175
- Wait... - Why're you tapping a transit card?

797
00:53:34,575 --> 00:53:35,845
Where's the key card?

798
00:53:38,875 --> 00:53:39,875
Am I dreaming?

799
00:53:40,515 --> 00:53:41,515
Step aside.

800
00:53:56,095 --> 00:53:57,095
I'm sorry.

801
00:54:00,805 --> 00:54:02,765
There's so much I want to say...

802
00:54:05,905 --> 00:54:07,375
and I'm sorry that this is all I can say.

803
00:54:08,375 --> 00:54:09,405
I'm sorry.

804
00:54:13,745 --> 00:54:15,545
What else do you want to say?

805
00:54:19,285 --> 00:54:20,455
I like you.

806
00:54:25,325 --> 00:54:27,195
The fact that it hurts to even say this...

807
00:54:30,265 --> 00:54:32,095
means I'm really being punished.

808
00:54:39,805 --> 00:54:40,905
You won't...

809
00:54:42,645 --> 00:54:43,775
remember this, will you?

810
00:54:44,545 --> 00:54:45,615
Should I...

811
00:54:46,985 --> 00:54:48,115
remember?

812
00:54:51,615 --> 00:54:52,785
If you tell me to, I will.

813
00:54:54,555 --> 00:54:56,355
And if you tell me not to, I won't.

814
00:55:05,965 --> 00:55:06,965
I know...

815
00:55:08,535 --> 00:55:10,635
that there's something between us.

816
00:55:12,235 --> 00:55:13,945
Keep liking me...

817
00:55:15,845 --> 00:55:16,975
and suffer the consequences.

818
00:55:36,695 --> 00:55:37,735
I will...

819
00:55:39,795 --> 00:55:40,805
remember.

820
00:55:46,435 --> 00:55:48,645
Stop. Hey.

821
00:55:55,215 --> 00:55:56,855
Cut. Hold on.

822
00:55:59,585 --> 00:56:00,585
DP.

823
00:56:00,985 --> 00:56:02,324
What do you think about going handheld...

824
00:56:02,325 --> 00:56:03,855
for this alley chase scene?

825
00:56:04,095 --> 00:56:06,895
- Good. - You've got to be kidding me.

826
00:56:07,665 --> 00:56:09,895
You want us to run with the camera for this entire scene?

827
00:56:10,095 --> 00:56:12,634
No, that's impossible. It'll mess up the actors' blocking.

828
00:56:12,635 --> 00:56:14,205
And the crew will keep getting in the shot. It won't work.

829
00:56:14,505 --> 00:56:16,434
For this scene, I want the audience to feel...

830
00:56:16,435 --> 00:56:18,475
like they're being chased along with Mu Gyeom.

831
00:56:18,635 --> 00:56:20,075
We need to build up the tension,

832
00:56:20,135 --> 00:56:23,245
so the scene where Crow rescues him will have more impact.

833
00:56:24,445 --> 00:56:26,075
Let's just try it once in rehearsal.

834
00:56:26,145 --> 00:56:28,545
If it absolutely doesn't work, I'll give up on it.

835
00:56:32,085 --> 00:56:33,085
Once.

836
00:56:33,685 --> 00:56:34,685
Thank you.

837
00:56:36,055 --> 00:56:37,295
All right, let's go handheld.

838
00:56:37,595 --> 00:56:39,755
Yes. Ye Seo, where are you?

839
00:56:40,525 --> 00:56:42,195
Yes, the actor has just arrived...

840
00:56:49,805 --> 00:56:50,805
Yi Jae.

841
00:56:52,305 --> 00:56:54,105
What was that? Are you all right?

842
00:56:54,775 --> 00:56:55,905
Who was that? Who did it?

843
00:56:56,375 --> 00:56:57,445
I'm sorry.

844
00:57:11,425 --> 00:57:12,425
That was dangerous.

845
00:57:18,565 --> 00:57:19,565
Director Joo.

846
00:57:19,895 --> 00:57:21,105
Seong Moo?

847
00:58:08,345 --> 00:58:10,385
(Dream To You)

848
00:58:10,555 --> 00:58:12,085
How did you feel when you heard I was coming?

849
00:58:12,415 --> 00:58:13,515
That's enough.

850
00:58:14,085 --> 00:58:16,525
You already know about Yi Jae and me.

851
00:58:16,585 --> 00:58:19,325
He was her first love?

852
00:58:19,455 --> 00:58:20,524
I love you.

853
00:58:20,525 --> 00:58:22,025
You don't remember that day, do you?

854
00:58:22,095 --> 00:58:23,095
You've had enough to drink.

855
00:58:23,325 --> 00:58:25,564
I wonder how far I can go using being drunk as an excuse.

856
00:58:25,565 --> 00:58:27,265
It's just the two of us here.

857
00:58:27,335 --> 00:58:29,565
- So you can be honest. - Don't you remember this place?

858
00:58:30,205 --> 00:58:31,635
Whether ten years ago or now...

859
00:58:32,135 --> 00:58:33,475
I still feel the same way about you.

860
00:58:33,975 --> 00:58:36,145
Are you still not over your first love?